    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105790" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τρωγοδύτις</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῠ</span>]  (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τρωγλ</span>-codd.), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδος</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Plu.
			2.939d
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Ael.
			<u>NA</u>
			17.3
		</span></i>:—the spelling <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τρωγλο-</span></b>  (as if <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Cave-dwellers</i>) is known to <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				1.2.34
			</span></i> (unless the passage is interpolated) and is freq. f.l.
				in codd. (so always in codd.<i><span class="en">
				Str.
			</span></i>, as <i><span class="en">
				16.4.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				17.1.13
			</span></i>, al., although he wrote it <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνευ τοῦ
				λ</span> acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				<u>Chr.</u>
				16.55
			</span></i>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				597a9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				2.160
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
